  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 251 AM EDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nTemps will return to the mid 90s by the middle of the week with \nwidespread triple digit heat index values along and south of I-85. A \nheat advisory may be needed for the southern portions of the CWA on \nThursday and Friday.\n\nOvernight lows will also be on the rise with the return of the mid \n70s to much of the area. This doesn't do much in providing relief \nfrom the daytime heat; especially for vulnerable populations. Look \nafter each other, and keep an eye on pets and kids. Stay hydrated if \nyou plan to spend time outside.\n\nThunderstorm chances during the afternoon will be down to less than \n2 0% for much of the area through the week. A weak front is expected \nnext weekend which will bring pops up to around 30%. Kept pops to \nless than categorical due to uncertainty.",
